-- title:
--   Entry and return contract for linking into a larger program.
-- statement:
--   Entry and return contract for linking into a larger program. The kernel
--   returns just before its halt and preserves every scalar at or above `k+12`
--   and every address at or above 6.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.framed_raw_halt`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.logProxyProgram_bounded_run`, `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.logProxyProgram_trace_from`.
